<%
  description = "Learn how to fit song lyrics on one page using font size, columns, spacing, and print preview, then create a clean lyric sheet."
%>
<% content_for :title, "Print Lyrics on One Page | PrintLyrics" %>
<% content_for :description, description %>
<% content_for :canonical_url, print_lyrics_on_one_page_url %>
<% content_for :robots, "index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1" %>

<div class="guide-shell">
  <article class="guide">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">A practical printing guide</p>
      <h1>Print lyrics on one page</h1>
      <p>Start with the clearest layout you can read comfortably, then make small adjustments until the print preview fits.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li>
        <h2>Start with the complete lyrics</h2>
        <p>Search for the song or paste your own text. Remove repeated notes or extra blank lines only when they are not useful while playing, teaching, or singing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Try two columns</h2>
        <p>Two columns often fit verses and choruses more naturally than one long column. They also reduce the distance your eyes travel across the page.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Reduce font size gradually</h2>
        <p>Choose the smallest font size that remains easy to read from where the page will sit. Avoid shrinking everything before trying columns.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Check print preview</h2>
        <p>Browser and printer margins vary. Open print preview before printing and confirm that the final lines remain on the first sheet.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section class="guide-callout" aria-labelledby="guide-tool-heading">
      <h2 id="guide-tool-heading">Make your lyric sheet</h2>
      <p>PrintLyrics lets you search or paste lyrics, review the text, choose a size and column layout, and print. No account is required.</p>
      <%= link_to "Open the lyric printing tool", root_path, class: "button button-primary" %>
    </section>
  </article>

  <%= render "shared/resource_navigation", current_section: :guide %>
</div>
